From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:37:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): add passkey (WebAuthn) sign-in

Add passkeys as an additional login method next to the password. Credentials
are discoverable (resident keys), so signing in needs no username: the
authenticator returns the userHandle embedded at registration.

- Server: RP configuration lives in a new `studio_settings` key/value table and
  is read on every ceremony, so administrators can change it without a restart.
  Credentials go in `webauthn_credentials`, keyed by SHA-256 of the credential id
  to keep the unique index short.
- Challenges are single-use, in-memory and expire after five minutes. Credentials
  persist in SQLite, so passkeys survive a restart.
- RP config is validated on write: bare hostname only, and every origin must sit
  within the RP ID. A mismatch here is what browsers report as an unexplained
  "unknown error" on phones, so failing early is the whole point.
- Client: the login view shows the passkey entry only when the instance is
  configured and at least one passkey exists, and account settings manage the
  signed-in user's own credentials. Super administrators also get the RP form.
- Errors are classified by message text, not only DOMException name, because
  @simplewebauthn/browser replaces the exception with its own wording. Without
  this the user sees "The authenticator was unable to process the specified
  options" instead of a hint about the domain.

Password login is untouched and remains the primary path.
